From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 07 Aug 2026 16:21:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: avoid clearing VHT160 support on width downgrade

hostapd_event_ch_switch() cleared the VHT width mask on every
channel switch and set it back only for 160 and 80+80 MHz landings,
so any other landing (including 320 MHz, which matches neither
branch) stripped the advertised VHT160 support. The clearing is
sticky: hostapd_reload_config() copies the runtime vht_capab over
every fresh parse and the ucode reload paths never replace the
radio config, so only a full interface re-add recovers. Until then
the beacon and probe response advertise no 160 MHz support,
connected STAs store the crippled AP capabilities and cannot follow
a later switch back up to 160 MHz, and hostapd_get_vht_capab()
strips 160 MHz from every new association. Drop the clear; the bits
are only ever set again.

With the clear removed, a [VHT160-80PLUS80] configuration that
later lands on 160 MHz would accumulate both width-mask bits (a
reserved value); we never operate 80+80, so this is theoretical.
The HT40 clear a few lines up stays: HT is handled symmetrically on
every ch_switch event and self-heals on the next switch.

Based-on-work-by: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/drv_callbacks.c |    1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
+++ b/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
@@ -1416,7 +1416,6 @@ void hostapd_event_ch_switch(struct host
 	hapd->iconf->punct_bitmap = punct_bitmap;
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 	if (hapd->iconf->ieee80211ac) {
-		hapd->iconf->vht_capab &= ~VHT_CAP_SUPP_CHAN_WIDTH_MASK;
 		if (chwidth == CONF_OPER_CHWIDTH_160MHZ)
 			hapd->iconf->vht_capab |=
 				VHT_CAP_SUPP_CHAN_WIDTH_160MHZ;
